    "story": "The foxhole is not deep enough, and he knows it.\n\nHe is down in the dirt with his back against the wall of the hole. The earth shakes under him from the shelling, and dirt rains down into his collar and his mouth, and the hole he dug is already half full again.\n\nThe submachine gun is across his knees, and his hands are on it. The hole is where he is, and the hole is where he stays.",
    "notes": "This one is a hole in the ground, and that is the point: a German soldier slumped in a foxhole, steel helmet and submachine gun, the dirt wall behind him doing the work of a landscape. The open mouth and the lean-back posture give the frame its urgency, and the pale earth against the dark uniform gives it its contrast. Collectors who want a WWII image that is about the dug-in war — the hole, the dirt, and the man in it — will find this one has it, plain and simple.",
