    "title": "Ready, Aim",
    "description": "A line of WWII soldiers kneels in tall grass with rifles aimed in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. In the foreground a soldier in a steel helmet kneels and aims his rifle across the field, while the men behind him — kneeling and prone in the grass — hold the same line, their rifles trained on the treeline at the far end. The wet grass, the low crouch of the line, and the stillness before the shot give the image its tension: a firing line caught in the breath before it fires.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA firing line in the grass, and the shot not yet taken. © Wayne Heim",
