    "id": "i-VNXbdGD",
    "title": "With the Tank",
    "description": "WWII soldiers advance alongside a tank in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. In the foreground a soldier in a steel helmet moves forward at a crouch with his rifle across his body, while the men behind him work their way out from behind sandbag walls and a tank grinds forward in the background, its gun pointed down the road. Smoke, cut-up ground, and the low crouch of the advance give the image its urgency: infantry and armor moving together, caught in the open.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nInfantry and armor, moving together through the smoke. © Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "WWII soldiers advancing with a tank in black and white, a lead soldier crouching forward with a rifle while men work their way out from behind sandbag walls and a tank follows behind, painterly fine art World War II battle photography by Wayne Heim",
