    "story": "He is out in front of the tank, moving at a crouch through the smoke with his rifle across his body, and the engine is loud enough to feel in his chest. The men behind him are still working their way out of the sandbags.\n\nThe tank is grinding forward behind them all, its gun pointed down the road ahead. He keeps his eyes forward and lets the noise stay behind him.\n\nThe road ahead is open and the smoke hangs over it in a way that hides what is on it. He keeps moving because the tank can cover the road but it cannot walk it for him.",
    "notes": "Armor changes everything in a frame like this: the tank in the background gives the infantry's advance a weight no foot soldier can give it alone, and the lead man's crouch — ahead of the armor, out in front of it all — is the nerve of the image. The sandbag walls, the smoke, and the cut-up ground fill out a scene that feels caught mid-movement rather than posed, and the black and white treatment keeps the tank's bulk and the men's low shapes in the same hard light. For a collector who wants the combined-arms war, infantry and armor together, this is the frame.",
