    "title": "At His Side",
    "description": "A WWII medic tends a wounded soldier lying in the grass in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The medic kneels over the prone man with his hands on his chest, leaning in close, while another soldier kneels behind them watching, and more men lie flat in the grass beyond. The long grass, the low crouch of the medic, and the stillness of the wounded man give the image its gravity: field aid in the open, with nothing between the men and the ground they are lying on.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA medic at work, and a man holding on. © Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A WWII medic kneeling over a wounded soldier lying in the grass in black and white, hands on the man's chest, another soldier kneeling behind them, painterly fine art World War II battle photography by Wayne Heim",
    "buyLink": "https://wayne-heim.smugmug.com/Galleries/Painterly-Fine-Art-Photography/Facing-History/WWII/War/Black-White/i-69rmhkz/A",

