    "story": "The strap will not sit right, and he keeps pulling at it with one hand while the pouches knock against his belt. A small wrongness, and it is filling his head because there is nothing bigger to think about yet.\n\nBehind him the other man is standing with his hands in his pockets and his sunglasses on, looking down the road they came up. Neither of them is talking. The smoke is thin this morning, and the ground is still quiet.\n\nHe gives the strap one more pull and leaves it where it falls. The road ahead is the same road it was a minute ago, and the pouches are still heavy, and the man behind him is still standing there. None of that is going to change before they move.",
    "notes": "A portrait inside a war set: a young German soldier adjusting the strap across his chest, pouches at his belt, and behind him a second man in sunglasses, hands in his pockets, watching the road. The smoke, the pale ground, and the pair's stillness give the frame a quiet that most of the advance frames skip, and the black and white treatment lets the uniforms and the faces carry the detail — no action, just two men, a strap, and the road. For a collector who wants the war's quieter register, the men rather than the fighting, this is a strong frame.",
