    "description": "A young WWII soldier in a netted steel helmet signals with a raised hand in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier kneels behind a low earth bank, his right arm raised and his mouth open as he calls out, a dark patch on his sleeve and his rifle slung at his back. The open mouth, the raised hand, and the dirt on his uniform give the image its urgency: a signal given in the open, with the men behind him out of frame.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA raised hand, and a voice carrying. © Wayne Heim",
