    "description": "A WWII soldier in a camouflage smock and beret walks through the haze in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier carries a rifle across his body and a large white kit bag slung across his chest, his smock damp at the shoulders, while two more soldiers stand behind him, half-lost in the haze. The white bag, the haze, and the men's low shapes give the image its tension: a patrol moving through ground that hides as much as it shows.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA white bag in the haze, and a patrol moving through it. © Wayne Heim",
