    "description": "A WWII soldier kneels on one knee in the grass with his rifle planted beside him in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier wears a steel helmet and a full pack, a patch on his sleeve, and looks off to the left while the rifle stands upright in the grass and the trees stand still behind him. The kneeling pose, the planted rifle, and the quiet field give the image its gravity: a pause on the move, held on one knee.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nOne knee in the grass, and the field holding still. © Wayne Heim",
