    "story": "He has stopped, and the others have not. They are moving past him in the background, and he is on one knee in the grass with the rifle across his body, both hands on it. His part of the morning is to stay where he is.\n\nThe rifle sits across his knees, and he keeps it there because it is where it belongs while he is down. The sun is on the back of his neck, and the air is still around him, and neither of them is a reason to move.\n\nThe men behind him are getting further away, and the field in front of him is the same field it was a minute ago. He is not following them. He is staying where he is, and the rifle is staying with him.",
