    "description": "A WWII soldier climbs over a large steel anti-tank obstacle in a smoky field in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier, in a steel helmet and full pack with his rifle slung on his back, has one boot on a beam of the crossed-steel obstacle while smoke fills the ground beyond it. The crossed steel, the smoke, and the man's mid-climb balance give the image its tension: an obstacle built for tanks, crossed by a man on foot.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nSteel built for tanks, crossed by a man. © Wayne Heim",
