    "title": "The Ford",
    "description": "Two WWII soldiers ford a shallow stream in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The lead soldier crouches in the water with his rifle held across his body, while the second soldier follows behind him, his rifle ready, both men wading through cold water toward a grassy far bank with a fence and a line of trees beyond. The cold water, the mud, and the low crouch of the crossing give the image its tension: a ford in the open, with the far bank still to reach.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nTwo men in the water, and the far bank still to reach. © Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "Two WWII soldiers fording a shallow stream in black and white, the lead soldier crouching in the water with a rifle across his body and a second soldier following behind, painterly fine art World War II battle photography by Wayne Heim",
