    "description": "A WWII soldier shouts with his fist raised high in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier, in a netted steel helmet with a grenade at his chest, holds a submachine gun in one hand and raises a clenched fist with the other, his mouth open, a stone wall at his back and smoke in front of him. The raised fist, the open mouth, and the weapon pointed at the sky give the image its force: a signal given loud, with the men behind him out of frame.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA fist in the air, and a voice behind it. © Wayne Heim",
