    "description": "A WWII soldier kneels behind a stone wall and points down at a prone comrade in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The soldier, in a netted steel helmet with a submachine gun in one hand, points with his other arm and shouts, while the man in the grass in the foreground lies face down, his rifle on his back. The stone wall, the wet grass, and the pointing arm give the image its tension: a man down in the open, and the men behind the wall learning about him.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA man down in the grass, and an arm pointing at him. © Wayne Heim",
