    "story": "The man in the grass is face down, and he is not moving. The rifle is still on his back and his helmet is still on his head, and from behind the wall, that is all there is to know about him.\n\nThe pointing man is up on his knees behind the wall, and he is telling the men who cannot see the grass what is in it. The wall is stone and the grass is wet, and the man in the grass has not moved since the pointing started.\n\nNobody behind the wall knows whether the man in the grass is down or done, and the pointing man does not know either. The arm stays out until somebody finds out.",
