    "story": "He is braced against the barrel with the rifle against his shoulder, and the barrel is holding him still. When the shot goes, the kick comes back into his shoulder and he takes it without moving, and the barrel does not move either.\n\nThe tree behind him is his cover from the back, and the barrel is his cover from the front, and between the two of them he has enough to do the job.\n\nThe shot is gone and the sound is still rolling across the grass, and he is already working the bolt for the next one. The first one found something or it found nothing, and the barrel is still there, and so is he.",
    "notes": "The barrel is the rest, and the man is the rifle — this frame is a study in bracing, a soldier crouched low behind an oak barrel with his rifle on its rim, the tree behind him and the grass open in front of him. The braced posture, the kick the rifle is about to give, and the stillness of the barrel give the image a tension the standing shots never find, and the black and white treatment keeps the barrel, the rifle, and the man's low shape at the front of the frame. For a collector who wants the shot itself — the firing, not the aiming — this is the moment to own.",
