    "title": "Doubling Up",
    "description": "Two WWII soldiers crouch behind a single wooden barrel in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The lead soldier, in a netted steel helmet, aims his rifle out across the grass from behind the barrel, while the second soldier leans over his back, half out in the open, a large pipe and a tree behind them. The shared barrel, the leaning man, and the grass around them give the image its tension: two men, one piece of cover, and the open ground on every side.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nTwo men, one barrel, and the open ground on every side. © Wayne Heim",
