    "description": "Two WWII soldiers crouch behind wooden barrels with a long rifle aimed across the grass in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The lead soldier, in a netted steel helmet, holds a long bolt-action rifle horizontally at shoulder height, its muzzle past the barrels, while the second soldier crouches behind him, a large pipe and a tree in the background. The long rifle, the wooden barrels, and the two men's low crouch give the image its tension: an aim held steady, with the shot still to come.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA long rifle held level, and the shot still to come. © Wayne Heim",
