    "description": "Two German soldiers lead a wounded comrade with bandaged eyes between them in this painterly World War II battle photograph by Wayne Heim, part of the Facing History collection. The wounded German soldier walks with a white bandage over his eyes, his head bowed, supported on one side by a German soldier in a steel helmet with a rifle on his back, and on the other by a German soldier in a field cap with a red-cross armband. The bandaged eyes, the two supporting hands, and the men's bowed heads give the image its gravity: a wounded man led by his comrades, with the ground ahead a place he cannot see.\n\nPart of a broader body of work, this piece is one of a series of images, crafted to honor the enduring legacy of the Facing History collection and the historical moments it represents. It is suited for collection within this narrative series, bringing depth, historical perspective, and emotion to any fine art collection or art lover's space.\n\nA wounded man between two comrades, and the dark in front of him. © Wayne Heim",
