    "story": "The half-track is coming up the sand and the sand is coming up with it — the tracks are throwing it, the tires are throwing it, and the men in the back are sitting in it, standing in it, leaning over the sides of it, and the back of it is full, and the full is the point.\n\nThe men in the back are standing, leaning, holding on to the sides, and the holding on is the ride — the half-track is moving, and the men are moving with it, and the men are all moving at the same speed, and the speed is the half-track's.\n\nThe front of the half-track is a face — the grille, the headlights, the star on the side, and the USA on the front — and the face is coming at the camera, and the back is full of men, and the men are the load, and the load is the half-track's job.",
    "notes": "Count the men in the back — a half-track packed with them, standing, sitting, leaning over the sides, the USA marking and the white star on the front, tire tracks in the sand behind it, the whole image in a vintage postcard-style treatment. The crowded back, the vehicle's face, and the sand give the image a momentum the tank frames never have, and the black and white treatment keeps the load and the sand at the front of the frame. For a collector who wants the ride — the half-track, the men, and the sand coming up with it — this one holds it.",
